WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.747
This practice turns bookstore business rules into
constraints Customer

00:00:05.774 --> 00:00:09.418
email must be present and unique so think about the
combination of

00:00:09.445 --> 00:00:15.009
NOT NULL and UNIQUE Order-item quantity must be
positive which is

00:00:15.035 --> 00:00:20.620
a CHECK rule Unit price cannot be negative which is
another CHECK

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:26.353
Every order item must reference an existing order
and book so foreign

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:32.704
keys are required Deletion behavior depends on
meaning Order

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.348
items may cascade when their order is deleted while
deleting a book

00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:41.734
that appears in historical orders may need to be
restricted Try naming

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.250
the constraint type for each rule before opening the
sample patterns The

00:00:46.263 --> 00:00:50.552
important skill is translating business language
into database-enforced rules
